Before the code — the flaw in "+1 year on every bootstrap":

Bootstrap runs once per realm. A stamp set only there is a one-year timer with nothing to renew it, which is the failure you just hit, deferred. And it can't self-renew from the config path: modifying `krbPasswordExpiration` needs admin-level write on that attribute, so svc-ansible can't push out its own expiry.

So the persistent fix is the password policy. The +1y stamp goes in anyway — it clears any expiry already stamped on the entry before the policy existed, which a policy change won't do retroactively.

**ipa.yml**

```yaml
---
- name: FreeIPA server
  hosts: ipaserver
  become: true
  gather_facts: false

  environment:
    KRB5CCNAME: "FILE:/tmp/krb5cc_ansible_ipa"

  pre_tasks:
    - name: Ensure Kerberos Python bindings present
      ansible.builtin.dnf:
        name: python3-gssapi
        state: present
      tags: [always]

  roles:
    - role: freeipa_install
      tags: [never, bootstrap]

    - role: freeipa_config
      tags: [config, bootstrap]

  post_tasks:
    - name: Destroy credential cache
      ansible.builtin.command:
        cmd: kdestroy -c FILE:/tmp/krb5cc_ansible_ipa
      changed_when: false
      failed_when: false
      tags: [always]
```

**roles/freeipa_install/defaults/main.yml**

```yaml
